From 872cd40177d6e4dfc9a346de1b6d5f705d4db6b3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 10:10:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add visit logging + GPS check-in for Sales staff
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Real "My Visits" feature: a rep can log a visit to one of their
assigned dealers with notes and their current GPS location, from that
dealer's detail screen. The dashboard's "My Visits" card is now a real
list of recent visits (was "coming soon").

- New sales_visits table, RLS enabled with no client policies —
  everything goes through SECURITY DEFINER RPCs, same pattern as every
  other Sales-dashboard function so far.
- log_dealer_visit(): inserts a visit, re-checking the caller's scope
  first (can't log against a dealer outside their assigned list).
- get_my_visits(): the caller's own recent visits across all dealers,
  for the dashboard.
- get_dealer_visits(): visit history for one dealer (including
  teammates' visits within scope), for the detail screen.
- DealerDetail.jsx: "Log a Visit" form (notes + GPS capture via
  navigator.geolocation, same pattern AdminDealers already uses) and a
  "Recent Visits" list with a link to view each visit's location on
  the map. GPS denial/unavailability still logs the visit, just
  without a location.

Also includes get_dealer_detail_fix.sql (already applied directly in
Supabase) for the migration history to match what's live.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GxWPdEf21EL6SvRpGBbX8q
